KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ B under construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ M under construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ after construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Each vtable slot has a `@vcall_offset' field.  A thunk through which a
virtual base's table enters an overrider reads it instead of subtracting
the base's offset in the overrider's complete class; set_virtual_base_offsets
fills it in for the complete object's and the construction tables, and a
base-object constructor for the tables it builds at run time.
